<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Liberation Front (Greece)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1941–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as EAM</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Liberation Front (EAM) was the largest Greek resistance movement during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> occupation, founded in September 1941 under the leadership of the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Its army, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-peoples-liberation-army">ELAS</a>, controlled much of the mountainous interior by 1944. Its conflict with the British-backed government led to fighting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> in December 1944 and later to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-civil-war">Greek Civil War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-greece.jpg" alt="National Liberation Front (Greece)" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%CE%95%CE%91%CE%9Cafisa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
